    "permutation": "Shuffle phase labels across draws. Balls from one draw stay together. The p-value is (exceedances + 1) / (shuffles + 1).",
    "multiple_testing": "Benjamini\u2013Hochberg and Bonferroni on the permutation p-values. The pooled family is every association test across games. Model-versus-chance p-values are reported separately and are not in that family.",
    "model": "The lottery transformer trains on earlier draws and is scored on the latest temporal holdout. Lunar columns are optional covariates for the draw being predicted. Tickets are rounded into a legal set of white balls. Chance is the expected overlap of a uniform ticket, plus one seeded random ticket.",
